9c4cb5e6acdff3" :answer/id #uuid "2d8f4a61-6240-5aac-94e8-814383d4cceb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-9" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-138784/field-4" :answer-field/id #uuid "0fb9d0ac-b069-5590-9b79-3ab3faea198b" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-138784/field-4/10293ac0295e0e79554137a949f5c5c46b9812dcc0a3ecb6349c4cb5e6acdff3" :answer-field/choices ["q-138784/field-4/10293ac0295e0e79554137a949f5c5c46b9812dcc0a3ecb6349c4cb5e6acdff3"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-138784" :question/id #uuid "c89b287d-33ff-50df-954b-524d0b0a1926" :question/math-academy-id "q-138784" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995865/assets/c1d9f53c6aed4acd378f8554df5c8beaaea81e169b5284e51f87204a87b3d53d.png)\n\nA housing complex designed by an architect is shown in the coordinate plane as the region $R$ with vertices $ABCD.$ A highway lies on the line $l$ with equation $2x+y+1=0.$ The area of the complex is $16$ hectares.\n\nEarlier part 1:\n\n$$\nX+Y=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\,Z=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrices above. Knowing that the matrix representation $T=[\\begin{aligned}{t}_{11} & {t}_{12} \\\\ {t}_{21} & {t}_{22}\\end{aligned}]$ of a linear transformation $T$ is given by\n\n$$\nT=XZ+YZ,\n$$\n\nfind the values ${t}_{ij}.$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ${t}_{11}=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $-3$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$\\,{t}_{12}=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $0$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                                \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ${t}_{21}=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $2$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$\\,{t}_{22}=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $-1$\n\nCurrent part:\n\nThe architect is expanding the plan of the housing complex. The transformation $T$ from part 1 maps the current plan of the housing complex $ABCD$ to the new plan ${A}^{′}{B}^{′}{C}^{′}{D}^{′}.$ Find the vertices of the new housing complex.\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ${A}^{′}(-9,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$)$\n$\\,$\n${B}^{′}($\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-2}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$,14)$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                                \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ${C}^{′}(-21,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-3}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$)$\n$\\,$\n${D}^{′}($\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-4}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$,0)$" :question/worked-solution "In part 1, we found that the matrix representation of $T$ is\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo find the image of the field under the action of $T,$ we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of $ABCD:$\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 7 & 7 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 4 & 6\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under the action of $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 & 7 & 7 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 4 & 6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-9 & -21 & -21 & -9 \\\\ 4 & 14 & 10 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective vertices ${A}^{′}{B}^{′}{C}^{′}{D}^{′}$ are $(-9,4),$ $(-21,14),$ $(-21,10),$ and $(-9,0),$ as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995865/assets/7430fd0c1e3a4c94e951eb1cf133e5c155f7a7b605a46b4b2272bf30fbb688e2.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-138784/field-1" "q-138784/field-2" "q-138784/field-3" "q-138784/field-4"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7c9849b9-397b-5fb9-bb4b-01f3d013c5c2"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-138784"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-138788/field-1/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "ba6081fd-7ac0-58e2-b2d7-ec659c2b6e2a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-138788/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "bccddd7d-1c52-572c-a2cc-102594d02482" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-138788/field-1/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer-field/choices ["q-138788/field-1/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-138788/field-2/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer/id #uuid "73f62ad2-f89e-5d66-bb92-d527a7e10faa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-138788/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "b6ccc186-6cfc-5081-a9d7-629f052fc633" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-138788/field-2/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer-field/choices ["q-138788/field-2/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-138788/field-3/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "9f7986e7-a3d4-51d6-bf0a-7e2c666c1c65" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-138788/field-3" :answer-field/id #uuid "fd14c748-8d0f-56f2-ae76-a6a276b9790d" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-138788/field-3/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer-field/choices ["q-138788/field-3/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-138788" :question/id #uuid "1adb0910-f5fb-5628-a732-8b56d7282ce1" :question/math-academy-id "q-138788" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995865/assets/c1d9f53c6aed4acd378f8554df5c8beaaea81e169b5284e51f87204a87b3d53d.png)\n\nA housing complex designed by an architect is shown in the coordinate plane as the region $R$ with vertices $ABCD.$ A highway lies on the line $l$ with equation $2x+y+1=0.$ The area of the complex is $16$ hectares.\n\nEarlier part 1:\n\n$$\nX+Y=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\,Z=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrices above. Knowing that the matrix representation $T=[\\begin{aligned}{t}_{11} & {t}_{12} \\\\ {t}_{21} & {t}_{22}\\end{aligned}]$ of a linear transformation $T$ is given by\n\n$$\nT=XZ+YZ,\n$$\n\nfind the values ${t}_{ij}.$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ${t}_{11}=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $-3$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$\\,{t}_{12}=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $0$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                                \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ${t}_{21}=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $2$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$\\,{t}_{22}=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $-1$\n\nEarlier part 2:\n\nThe architect is expanding the plan of the housing complex. The transformation $T$ from part 1 maps the current plan of the housing complex $ABCD$ to the new plan ${A}^{′}{B}^{′}{C}^{′}{D}^{′}.$ Find the vertices of the new housing complex.\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ${A}^{′}(-9,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $4$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$)$\n$\\,$\n${B}^{′}($\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $-21$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$,14)$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                                \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ${C}^{′}(-21,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $10$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$)$\n$\\,$\n${D}^{′}($\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $-9$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$,0)$\n\nEarlier part 3:\n\nThe area of the new housing complex is\n\n                            \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $48$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \nhectares.\n\nEarlier part 4:\n\nA triangular recreational area next to the housing complex is mapped to a larger recreational area under the action of $T.$ The larger recreational area has vertices ${L}^{′}(-15,4),$ ${M}^{′}(-15,2),$ and ${N}^{′}(-21,6).$ Find the corresponding vertices of the smaller recreational area.\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $L(5,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $6$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$)$\n$\\,$\n$M($\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $5$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$,8)$\n$\\,$\n$N(7,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $8$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$)$\n\nEarlier part 5:\n\nThe architect finds the image of the line $l$ under the action of $T$ and places another highway on the plan from this image. The equation of the line on which the new highway lies, in **standard form**, is\n\n                            \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $4$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$x\\,+\\,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $3$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$y\\,=\\,3.$\n\nCurrent part:\n\nThe solution of the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2x+y+1=0 \\\\ 4x+3y-3=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\ngives the point where the highways meet. This solution can be written in matrix form as\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ -4 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ c\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nFind the values of $a,$ $b,$ and $c.$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $a\\,=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$\\,b\\,=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-2}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$\\,c\\,=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-3}}" :question/worked-solution "This system can be written as\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo find the solution, we need to calculate the inverse of the coefficient matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 3\\end{aligned}].$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{2\\cdot 3-4\\cdot 1}[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ -4 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ -4 & 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the solution to this system as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ -4 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-138788/field-1" "q-138788/field-2" "q-138788/field-3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c89778fa-3c8d-5f0a-a0f8-c9b3d9193ffd"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-138788"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-138786/field-1/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" :answer/id #uuid "2373e93f-3a70-5dc9-8f11-0d3001ec0b62" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-138786/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "81f84f96-477c-5c7b-ab0d-eb1f36f66952" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-138786/field-1/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" :answer-field/choices ["q-138786/field-1/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-138786/field-2/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" :answer/id #uuid "f52b1deb-f129-59d5-8afa-fa9c9e8e07a3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q