            \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ${t}_{11}=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $-3$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$\\,{t}_{12}=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $0$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                                \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ${t}_{21}=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $2$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$\\,{t}_{22}=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $-1$\n\nEarlier part 2:\n\nThe architect is expanding the plan of the housing complex. The transformation $T$ from part 1 maps the current plan of the housing complex $ABCD$ to the new plan ${A}^{′}{B}^{′}{C}^{′}{D}^{′}.$ Find the vertices of the new housing complex.\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ${A}^{′}(-9,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $4$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$)$\n$\\,$\n${B}^{′}($\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $-21$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$,14)$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                                \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ${C}^{′}(-21,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $10$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$)$\n$\\,$\n${D}^{′}($\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $-9$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$,0)$\n\nEarlier part 3:\n\nThe area of the new housing complex is\n\n                            \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $48$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \nhectares.\n\nCurrent part:\n\nA triangular recreational area next to the housing complex is mapped to a larger recreational area under the action of $T.$ The larger recreational area has vertices ${L}^{′}(-15,4),$ ${M}^{′}(-15,2),$ and ${N}^{′}(-21,6).$ Find the corresponding vertices of the smaller recreational area.\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $L(5,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$)$\n$\\,$\n$M($\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-2}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$,8)$\n$\\,$\n$N(7,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-3}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$)$" :question/worked-solution "In part 1, we found that the matrix representation of $T$ is\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFirst, we create a matrix $Y$ containing all of the vertices of the larger recreational area:\n\n$$\nY=[\\begin{aligned}-15 & -15 & -21 \\\\ 4 & 2 & 6\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nNow, if $X$ denotes the matrix that contains the corresponding vertices of the smaller recreational area, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T\\cdot X & =Y \\\\ T\\cdot X & =[\\begin{aligned}-15 & -15 & -21 \\\\ 4 & 2 & 6\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe need to reverse the action of the matrix $T.$ So, we multiply the above equation by ${T}^{-1},$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{-1}\\cdot T\\cdot X & ={T}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-15 & -15 & -21 \\\\ 4 & 2 & 6\\end{aligned}] \\\\ X & ={T}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-15 & -15 & -21 \\\\ 4 & 2 & 6\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe inverse of $T$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{(-1)(-3)-0}[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & -3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & -3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X & ={T}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-15 & -15 & -21 \\\\ 4 & 2 & 6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & -3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-15 & -15 & -21 \\\\ 4 & 2 & 6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}15 & 15 & 21 \\\\ 18 & 24 & 24\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}5 & 5 & 7 \\\\ 6 & 8 & 8\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the vertices of the smaller recreational area are $L(5,6),$ $M(5,8),$ and $N(7,8).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-138786/field-1" "q-138786/field-2" "q-138786/field-3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b0cbb889-0fe1-5347-94a3-53db3ff9a95c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-138786"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-138785/field-1/cee37ae0a2921bd3973a5cb0592c822dbbfafcfefba8d7007910ead797b9112f" :answer/id #uuid "4dae3b81-42bf-5d8f-a573-f4e8f864bcf8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "48" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-138785/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "9f12e676-d778-55a6-bc23-f52756889a29" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-138785/field-1/cee37ae0a2921bd3973a5cb0592c822dbbfafcfefba8d7007910ead797b9112f" :answer-field/choices ["q-138785/field-1/cee37ae0a2921bd3973a5cb0592c822dbbfafcfefba8d7007910ead797b9112f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-138785" :question/id #uuid "6bb7d03d-675a-5ff1-80f4-70e2c7657223" :question/math-academy-id "q-138785" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995865/assets/c1d9f53c6aed4acd378f8554df5c8beaaea81e169b5284e51f87204a87b3d53d.png)\n\nA housing complex designed by an architect is shown in the coordinate plane as the region $R$ with vertices $ABCD.$ A highway lies on the line $l$ with equation $2x+y+1=0.$ The area of the complex is $16$ hectares.\n\nEarlier part 1:\n\n$$\nX+Y=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\,Z=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrices above. Knowing that the matrix representation $T=[\\begin{aligned}{t}_{11} & {t}_{12} \\\\ {t}_{21} & {t}_{22}\\end{aligned}]$ of a linear transformation $T$ is given by\n\n$$\nT=XZ+YZ,\n$$\n\nfind the values ${t}_{ij}.$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ${t}_{11}=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $-3$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$\\,{t}_{12}=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $0$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                                \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ${t}_{21}=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $2$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$\\,{t}_{22}=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $-1$\n\nEarlier part 2:\n\nThe architect is expanding the plan of the housing complex. The transformation $T$ from part 1 maps the current plan of the housing complex $ABCD$ to the new plan ${A}^{′}{B}^{′}{C}^{′}{D}^{′}.$ Find the vertices of the new housing complex.\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ${A}^{′}(-9,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $4$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$)$\n$\\,$\n${B}^{′}($\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $-21$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$,14)$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                                \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ${C}^{′}(-21,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $10$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$)$\n$\\,$\n${D}^{′}($\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $-9$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$,0)$\n\nCurrent part:\n\nThe area of the new housing complex is\n\n                            \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \nhectares." :question/worked-solution "Recall that for any linear transformation $T,$ we have the following connection between the area of $R$ (the old housing complex) and the area of the image $T(R)$ (the new housing complex) under the action of $T:$\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(T(R))=|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(R)\n$$\n\nWe're given that\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(R)=16\\,\\text{hectares}.\n$$\n\nComputing the determinant of the matrix $T$ (found in part 1), we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(T) & =|\\begin{aligned}-3 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(-3)\\cdot (-1)-(2)\\cdot 0 \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(T(R)) & =|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(R) \\\\  & =3\\cdot 16 \\\\  & =48.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of the new housing complex is $48$ hectares." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-138785/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4d59733f-3396-5d59-98a9-3f2e0ccfbbc4"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-138785"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-138783/field-1/b13ac151352392d38026eed875b911708c50c896d6c09463410ac041030163ff" :answer/id #uuid "65484580-edd7-5f93-83b3-5617ae5ce4ee" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-138783/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "7c6f41d7-f1c4-54af-b9ab-63f225b3f0d5" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-138783/field-1/b13ac151352392d38026eed875b911708c50c896d6c09463410ac041030163ff" :answer-field/choices ["q-138783/field-1/b13ac151352392d38026eed875b911708c50c896d6c09463410ac041030163ff"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-138783/field-2/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "3576992c-75d0-5e95-a2be-249f25e01e30" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-138783/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "3beb0fad-9ebe-5092-97b9-6ab515b6f281" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-138783/field-2/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer-field/choices ["q-138783/field-2/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-138783/field-3/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "8e40f2f1-9288-5d1e-ae0c-440f27368192" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-138783/field-3" :answer-field/id #uuid "d27d1c11-0014-5811-aa99-95e629e423b4" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-138783/field-3/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer-field/choices ["q-138783/field-3/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-138783/field-4/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer/id #uuid "f29572bc-a376-5e26-908c-dd4693b8b94a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-138783/field-4" :answer-field/id #uuid "36b1c7be-4271-51b0-b452-145e670ba402" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-138783/field-4/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer-field/choices ["q-138783/field-4/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-138783" :question/id #uuid "298f431b-16f6-54d9-a1a9-ec74c0465162" :question/math-academy-id "q-138783" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995865/assets/c1d9f53c6aed4acd378f8554df5c8beaaea81e169b5284e51f87204a87b3d53d.png)\n\nA housing complex designed by an architect is shown in the coordinate plane as the region $R$ with vertices $ABCD.$ A highway lies on the line $l$ with equation $2x+y+1=0.$ The area of the complex is $16$ hectares.\n\nCurrent part:\n\n$$\nX+Y=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\,Z=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrices above. Knowing that the matrix representation $T=[\\begin{aligned}{t}_{11} & {t}_{12} \\\\ {t}_{21} & {t}_{22}\\end{aligned}]$ of a linear transformation $T$ is given by\n\n$$\nT=XZ+YZ,\n$$\n\nfind the values ${t}_{ij}.$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ${t}_{11}=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$\\,{t}_{12}=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-2}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                                \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ${t}_{21}=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-3}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$\\,{t}_{22}=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-4}}" :question/worked-solution "We apply the distributive law\n\n$$\nXZ+YZ=(X+Y)Z.\n$$\n\nSo, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T & =XZ+YZ \\\\  & =(X+Y)Z \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-138783/field-1" "q-138783/field-2" "q-138783/field-3" "q-138783/field-4"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a7ad52ce-d408-5390-b91f-c855274f39ea"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-138783"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-138787/field-1/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "3b732e67-b272-5e0a-8135-7852163fc087" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-138787/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "ceaa648a-b074-51bc-bfb4-ab5cdff84d97" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-138787/field-1/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer-field/choices ["q-138787/field-1/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-138787/field-2/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "29c3f4c8-0685-5108-986f-da507127ad10" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-138787/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "da63ed26-2492-5299-83d6-3c95f9cd36d7" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-138787/field-2/62a6fd1cf465955ce