                                     \n$\\,{t}_{12}=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $0$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                                \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ${t}_{21}=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $2$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$\\,{t}_{22}=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $-1$\n\nEarlier part 2:\n\nThe architect is expanding the plan of the housing complex. The transformation $T$ from part 1 maps the current plan of the housing complex $ABCD$ to the new plan ${A}^{′}{B}^{′}{C}^{′}{D}^{′}.$ Find the vertices of the new housing complex.\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ${A}^{′}(-9,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $4$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$)$\n$\\,$\n${B}^{′}($\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $-21$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$,14)$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                                \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ${C}^{′}(-21,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $10$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$)$\n$\\,$\n${D}^{′}($\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $-9$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$,0)$\n\nEarlier part 3:\n\nThe area of the new housing complex is\n\n                            \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $48$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \nhectares.\n\nEarlier part 4:\n\nA triangular recreational area next to the housing complex is mapped to a larger recreational area under the action of $T.$ The larger recreational area has vertices ${L}^{′}(-15,4),$ ${M}^{′}(-15,2),$ and ${N}^{′}(-21,6).$ Find the corresponding vertices of the smaller recreational area.\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $L(5,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $6$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$)$\n$\\,$\n$M($\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $5$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$,8)$\n$\\,$\n$N(7,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $8$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$)$\n\nCurrent part:\n\nThe architect finds the image of the line $l$ under the action of $T$ and places another highway on the plan from this image. The equation of the line on which the new highway lies, in **standard form**, is\n\n                            \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$x\\,+\\,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-2}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$y\\,=\\,3.$" :question/worked-solution "In part 1, we found that the matrix representation of $T$ is\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFirst, notice that the line $2x+y+1=0$ passes through the points $U(-1,1)$ and $V(0,-1)$ since the coordinates of both points satisfy the equation.\n\nTo find the image of $U$ and $V$ under the action of $T,$ we first create a matrix $X$ containing the coordinates of the points:\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under the action of $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective image points are ${U}^{′}(3,-3)$ and ${V}^{′}(0,1).$\n\nFinally, we write the equation of the line that passes through ${U}^{′}$ and ${V}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-{y}_{1} & =\\frac{{y}_{2}-{y}_{1}}{{x}_{2}-{x}_{1}}(x-{x}_{1}) \\\\ y-(-3) & =\\frac{1-(-3)}{0-3}(x-3) \\\\ y+3 & =-\\frac{4}{3}(x-3) \\\\ 3y+9 & =-4x+12 \\\\ 4x+3y+9 & =12 \\\\ 4x+3y & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-138787/field-1" "q-138787/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "15e8730b-c59a-5897-8c83-073b54f517a9"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-138787"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
